          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong Boolean topos
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            that is also a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
          %p There are several conditions on a topos that are necessary and sufficient to be Boolean:
          %ul
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
              has a complement (the general definition of Boolean category).
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+poset"} subobject lattice
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+algebra"} Boolean algebra
            %li
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              Boolean algebra.
            %li
              The maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top, \bot: 1 \to \Omega
              are a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              cone (so in particular,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo ≅
                      %mn 1
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \cong 1 + 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo ⊤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\top, \bot]: 1 + 1 \to \Omega
              is always a monomorphism, and any monic endomorphism of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is an automorphism).
            %li
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+object"} free
              pointed object. This was proven
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2023/01/freedom.html#c062002"} here
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morgan+Rogers"} Morgan Rogers
          %h3#warning Warning
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a Boolean pretopos, i.e. a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            in which is also a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+category"} Boolean category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+topos"} classifying topos
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em not
            follow that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
            is Boolean. In fact, this is rarely the case, even if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the classifying pretopos for a theory in classical first-order logic. See
            %a{:href => "#BlassScedrov75"} Blass and Scedrov
            for a characterization of which classical first-order theories have Boolean classifying topoi – in particular, any such theory is
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℵ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categoricity"} categorical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Barr%27s+theorem"} Barr's theorem
            shows that any topos admits a surjection from a Boolean topos.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_a_context_for_foundations As a context for foundations
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal logic
            of a Boolean topos with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            can serve as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/foundations"} foundations
            for “ordinary” mathematics, except for that which relies on the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+replacement"} axiom of replacement
            or an axiom of
            = succeed "s.)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+universe"} Grothendieck universe
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
            Boolean
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pretopos"} pretopos
            is in fact a topos. This is why ‘generalised
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicativism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            only.
          %h3#some_characterisations Some characterisations
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
